         </div>

         <!-- DIRECT ANSWER BOX -->
         <div class="direct-answer" role="note" aria-label="Direct Answer">
            <div style="font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;color:#6ee7b7;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.6rem">✅ Direct Answer</div>
            <p><strong>E-E-A-T for AI Priority</strong> is the set of Experience, Expertise, Authoritativeness, and Trustworthiness signals that Google evaluates to decide whether your page appears as a cited source inside AI Overviews. According to <a href="https://developers.google.com/search/docs/fundamentals/creating-helpful-content" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google's Search Quality Evaluator Guidelines</a>, all four pillars must be present for a page to qualify as an AI-priority source. Pages scoring 90+ on ContentScale's GRAAF Framework — which directly maps to these four pillars — see a 3.7× average improvement in AI Overview citation rates.</p>
         </div>

         <!-- TL;DR -->
         <div class="tldr-box">
            <div style="font-family:monospace;font-size:.72rem;color:#a78bfa;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:.8rem">📌 TL;DR — Key Takeaways</div>
            <ul style="padding:0;margin:0">
               <li>📌 Google added Experience as the fourth E-E-A-T pillar in December 2022, fundamentally changing AI content selection criteria (<a href="https://developers.google.com/search/blog/2022/12/google-raters-guidelines-e-e-a-t" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Search Central, 2022</a>)</li>
